  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 acc while image (ResNet50) is weak at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the PCA linear projection is the bottleneck or whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi) can extract more discriminative signal from the same RNA data. This experiment tests config_004 (RNA-only, single profile, scvi_n200), which is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001—only the encoder changes. If scvi substantially improves over PCA, we know learned representations are critical and should prioritize the best encoder for all downstream multimodal experiments; if it is comparable or worse, PCA is sufficient and we can redirect remaining budget toward multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. With 7 experiments left, resolving the encoder question early is the highest-information, lowest-risk step before committing to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

